A||||4||Ronen||headrest speaker question||||5||
Z||000000||Ronen||05-23-2001||06:49 PM||||My original Fiero GT V6 85 has speaker holes on the headrest. When I installed the radio from my newly delivered Fiero GT V6 85 spare parts car to my first Fiero the headrest speaker do not work. The question is: is there speakers in the headrest or did Pontiac put the holes there for looks, and the original owner did not buy the rear speakers option? I thought in 1985 rear speakers were standard equipment in all Fieros. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-23-2001||07:14 PM||||The headrest speakers were on ever 84 and 85 Fiero. I don't think there was one made without them. (Unless the car was specifically ordered with the radio delete option) It could be they are disconnected (or removed) because they went bad.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||05-23-2001||07:21 PM||||If you want to see if there are speakers in there do this:<P>unzipper bottom part, end/begining of zipper are tucked in<BR>start pulling up on the seat skin until youi see two medal rods in the front, pull the medal ruds off the connection things, strait down<BR>lift up until you get to the head rest<BR>pull the back part over to the front, take your time so you dont rip it (doing it this way you will not have to undo the front clips in front of the head rest) <P>a reason why they might now work could be possible someone put those seat skins over to replace ripped ones maybe?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||05-23-2001||09:26 PM||||Slide the seat forward !<BR>Rotate the seatback forward!<BR>LOOK over by the center console!<BR>There is a plug hanging out of the seat.<BR>Make sure it's pluged up<BR>I've never seen a seat speaker system fail.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ronen||05-24-2001||01:34 PM||||Found the problem. The wire disconnected itself when I tried putting the radio into the console. Its all fixed now with new connectors. THank you||||reg||1
